<%= render "pages/hero" %>
<%= render "pages/events", events: @events %>
<%= render "pages/sponsors", sponsors: @sponsors %>

<section class="bg-white py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-harbor-900 sm:text-4xl">
        Everyone is welcome here
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800 sm:text-lg">
        That isn't a slogan we put in the footer. Bmore on Rails is for career
        switchers, bootcamp grads, students, hobbyists, and people who've been
        writing Ruby for twenty years — often in the same room, on the same
        night.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-800 sm:text-lg">
        We hold ourselves to a code of conduct that we actually enforce. If
        something goes wrong at one of our events, there is a real person to
        tell and a real process behind it.
      </p>
      <%= link_to code_of_conduct_path,
            class: "mt-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-harbor-800 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-marble-50 transition hover:bg-harbor-700 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-harbor-500" do %>
        Read our code of conduct
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <dl class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-1 lg:gap-8">
      <div class="border-l-4 border-brick-500 pl-5">
        <dt class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-harbor-900">
          You don't need to know Ruby
        </dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-700">
          Curious counts. Come, listen, ask the "obvious" question — someone
          else in the room is wondering the same thing.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-gold-400 pl-5">
        <dt class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-harbor-900">
          It's always free
        </dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-700">
          No tickets, no membership. Our sponsors cover the space and the food
          so cost is never the reason you stayed home.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-4 border-harbor-500 pl-5">
        <dt class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-harbor-900">
          Come for one talk, stay for the people
        </dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 text-base leading-relaxed text-harbor-700">
          Baltimore's tech scene is small enough that you'll recognize faces by
          your second visit. That's the best part.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
